</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/af99d4e1e89b36140b037bba7b5a0941e045dc11" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:10.073ex; height:3.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \phi (s_{i})=s_{i}'}"/></span>. This means the associated moduli functor </p><blockquote id="mwaQ"><p id="mwag"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt48" id="mwaw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbf{P}^n_\\mathbb{Z}:\\text{Sch}\\to \\text{Sets}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbf {P} _{\mathbb {Z} }^{n}:{\text{Sch}}\to {\text{Sets}}}">
