</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/e5d7c191be99514e60f64b150442c982f13d5556" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -4.171ex; width:65.099ex; height:9.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbf {P} _{\mathbb {Z} }^{n}(X)=\left\{({\mathcal {L}},s_{0},\ldots ,s_{n}):{\begin{matrix}{\mathcal {L}}\to X{\text{ is a line bundle}}\\s_{0},\ldots ,s_{n}\in \Gamma (X,{\mathcal {L}})\\{\text{ form a basis of global sections}}\end{matrix}}\right\}/\sim }"/></span></p></blockquote><p id="mwcQ">Showing this is true can be done by running through a series of tautologies: any projective embedding <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt51" id="mwcg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"i:X \\to \\mathbb{P}^n_\\mathbb{Z}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle i:X\to \mathbb {P} _{\mathbb {Z} }^{n}}">
